&lt;p&gt;Want to lead AI development for the world’s largest competitive tactical shooter? As &lt;strong&gt;Engineering Manager&lt;/strong&gt; on the VALORANT team, you will guide a group of engineers building the systems, behaviors, and machine-learning–driven capabilities. You will lead a passionate team of engineers in supporting the ongoing needs of a large and geographically diverse development team. You will bring management and development experience, strong technical judgment, and a passion for advocating for both players and developers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a group of 4-8 engineers across experience levels, providing regular feedback and performance management. Coach and develop your engineering team to grow in their roles, develop technical skills, and improve their effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and communicate the technical vision for your team, working with design, production, and game leadership partners to ensure consistency with overall product goals. Communicate and evangelize this vision to your team clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for players, your team, and internal development customers when deciding what to build and why. Coordinate and work effectively with other teams across Riot working on AI and ML technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a technical backstop by contributing to code as appropriate, reviewing technical designs, and ensuring strong engineering practices and architectural rigor. Ensure high technical quality of what your team produces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a collaborative, challenging, and satisfying environment for your development team. Find and surface issues, opportunities, and address them head-on. Celebrate wins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a standard-bearer and role model of Riot values for your team and others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve conflict and respond to emergent issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Other reasonable activities required by management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
