&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of professional software engineering experience in mobile, game development, or related fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant professional experience developing and debugging native applications or systems on iOS and/or Android.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency with C++, including experience using C++ in a mobile, game, or performance-sensitive environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience diagnosing complex issues that cross application, engine, platform, and native-code boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience debugging, profiling, and optimizing mobile applications or games, including performance, memory, stability, and device-specific issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with a game engine such as Unreal Engine or Unity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead technical initiatives, make architectural decisions, and solve complex problems with broad or ambiguous requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating across disciplines such as Engineering, Design, Art, QA, and Production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work collaboratively with teams distributed across multiple time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product sense, pragmatism, and player empathy when making technical decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with iterative development methodologies such as Agile, Scrum, or equivalent development practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS in Computer Science, or proven understanding of Computer Science fundamentals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
